1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:05,000
(Previously) Why are you doing this? Isn't
it good that you returned to Prince Thin?

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:09,000
As long as I am alive,
you two will never be together!

3
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:13,000
In the end... is what I
chose really worth it?

4
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:16,500
P' Thin asked me to give this to you, Phob.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,700
Please don't leave me...

6
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:24,176
We've become two people
who can't love each other anymore, Phob.

7
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:25,200
Let go.

8
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:27,800
Good luck to you.

9
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:02,000
"The Edge of Horizon"
(Episode 9)

10
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:15,001
I love you.

11
00:02:18,097 --> 00:02:19,275
I love you, too.

12
00:02:20,966 --> 00:02:23,155
Even if I have to wait months, years,

13
00:02:23,649 --> 00:02:24,650
or the rest of my life,

14
00:02:25,446 --> 00:02:27,595
you're the only one I'll ever wait for.

15
00:02:28,982 --> 00:02:32,299
No matter what happens, I will forever be…

16
00:02:33,419 --> 00:02:34,420
your Phobthee.

17
00:02:38,915 --> 00:02:39,916
Tin, darling.

18
00:02:46,641 --> 00:02:47,642
Grandma.

19
00:02:48,902 --> 00:02:49,903
Grandma.

20
00:02:51,590 --> 00:02:52,591
Grandma.

21
00:02:58,358 --> 00:03:00,195
I went to see Phob.

22
00:03:01,553 --> 00:03:03,075
What did he say?

23
00:03:06,337 --> 00:03:08,875
He told me he wanted us to
go back to the way we were.

24
00:03:11,285 --> 00:03:12,286
To be the same?

25
00:03:12,779 --> 00:03:14,817
How could we go back to the way we were?

26
00:03:16,337 --> 00:03:17,675
How could we do that?

27
00:03:25,857 --> 00:03:26,958
You poor thing.

28
00:03:32,134 --> 00:03:35,085
I used to think the greatest obstacle
between Phop and me

29
00:03:35,566 --> 00:03:38,227
was that we were different
from everyone else,

30
00:03:38,995 --> 00:03:41,438
that society would never accept us.

31
00:03:42,115 --> 00:03:44,635
But I believed that
as long as we loved each other enough,

32
00:03:44,685 --> 00:03:46,686
we could face it together
and make it through.

33
00:03:47,155 --> 00:03:49,835
But today, I realized that
the problem was never anyone else.

34
00:03:49,856 --> 00:03:51,115
It was me.

35
00:03:51,523 --> 00:03:53,835
I'm the one he wants to change, Grandma.

36
00:03:53,924 --> 00:03:55,475
I'm part of the system he wants…

37
00:03:56,147 --> 00:03:58,195
he wants to dismantle.

38
00:03:59,374 --> 00:04:01,635
How can we be together?

39
00:04:01,675 --> 00:04:03,491
How can we be in love after this?

40
00:04:08,142 --> 00:04:09,875
It's okay, darling.

41
00:04:11,390 --> 00:04:12,873
You still have me.

42
00:04:13,270 --> 00:04:14,571
I'm right here with you.

43
00:04:17,222 --> 00:04:18,515
It's going to be okay, darling.

44
00:04:29,887 --> 00:04:30,888
Sakchai.

45
00:04:32,942 --> 00:04:33,943
Sakchai, hi.

46
00:04:35,035 --> 00:04:36,036
Where are you heading to?

47
00:04:37,419 --> 00:04:38,435
To the mine?

48
00:04:39,089 --> 00:04:40,435
Good, I'll go with you.

49
00:04:40,735 --> 00:04:43,395
Oh, come on! There is no mining business.

50
00:04:50,595 --> 00:04:52,526
Then how...

51
00:04:53,331 --> 00:04:54,611
how did we make a profit before?

52
00:04:55,379 --> 00:04:56,380
That money...

53
00:04:56,633 --> 00:04:58,987
was just bait to sucker
more idiots into investing.

54
00:05:04,150 --> 00:05:05,275
You fooled me?

55
00:05:08,422 --> 00:05:09,675
Are you lying to me?

56
00:05:11,051 --> 00:05:13,235
You son of a bitch!

57
00:05:13,387 --> 00:05:14,515
You fooled me?

58
00:05:14,867 --> 00:05:17,275
You lied to me! Do you
even know who I am, huh?

59
00:05:17,550 --> 00:05:18,595
How dare you lie to me?

60
00:05:31,505 --> 00:05:33,555
Do you know who you are now?

61
00:05:35,078 --> 00:05:37,315
Do you still think being
part of the royal family

62
00:05:37,646 --> 00:05:38,735
means anything anymore?

63
00:05:39,611 --> 00:05:43,235
If you still had any power,
you wouldn't be this desperate for money.

64
00:05:48,107 --> 00:05:50,753
That's the ministry's
money! It's the ministry money!

65
00:05:51,062 --> 00:05:52,735
Give me my money back.

66
00:05:53,089 --> 00:05:56,835
I'll go to jail if I don't have that money!
I have to pay it back!

67
00:05:57,190 --> 00:05:58,191
It's none of my business.

68
00:05:58,502 --> 00:06:01,155
You're stupid enough to steal the money!

69
00:06:01,735 --> 00:06:02,736
Go!

70
00:06:03,595 --> 00:06:05,435
Hey!

71
00:06:05,507 --> 00:06:06,795
Don't go! Give me the money!

72
00:06:07,475 --> 00:06:09,795
Give me the money, Sakchai!

73
00:06:15,401 --> 00:06:17,595
I don't want to go to jail!

74
00:06:29,494 --> 00:06:32,166
Chat, darling. Wait.

75
00:06:32,390 --> 00:06:33,772
What happened to you? Why did you look like this?

76
00:06:33,796 --> 00:06:34,995
Grandma.

77
00:06:35,025 --> 00:06:36,715
I'm so exhausted, I need to rest.

78
00:06:36,755 --> 00:06:38,675
Tell me what is going on?

79
00:06:38,806 --> 00:06:41,435
M.C. Chatthorn Varakulvatin,

80
00:06:42,134 --> 00:06:44,835
You have been charged with embezzling funds

81
00:06:45,109 --> 00:06:46,875
from the Ministry of Finance.

82
00:06:50,222 --> 00:06:51,782
What kind of ridiculous charge is that?

83
00:06:52,691 --> 00:06:54,235
My son is not an embezzler.

84
00:06:54,587 --> 00:06:59,341
The People's Committee of Siam audited the
accounts Prince Chatthorn was responsible for,

85
00:06:59,499 --> 00:07:01,795
and found that as much
as 200,000 baht was missing.

86
00:07:05,467 --> 00:07:07,515
Phob is trying to attack on us.

87
00:07:08,139 --> 00:07:09,640
He is framing my son.

88
00:07:10,646 --> 00:07:13,006
He has been fired,
how could he embezzle from the ministry?

89
00:07:14,755 --> 00:07:16,335
And we're talking about 200,000 baht.

90
00:07:17,070 --> 00:07:19,115
If you're saying Chat really took
the money, do you have any proof?

91
00:07:19,139 --> 00:07:20,835
All the evidence is at the police station.

92
00:07:21,102 --> 00:07:23,955
I suggest you cooperate and come with me.

93
00:07:24,182 --> 00:07:25,403
Officer, take him.

94
00:07:25,558 --> 00:07:26,559
No!

95
00:07:26,998 --> 00:07:28,115
Dad! Grandma!

96
00:07:28,283 --> 00:07:31,155
Dad! Don't let them do this to me! Dad!

97
00:07:31,297 --> 00:07:32,515
Dad! Help me!

98
00:07:33,438 --> 00:07:35,515
Oh my! Your Highness!

99
00:07:47,387 --> 00:07:48,388
Phob, I have bad news.

100
00:07:48,595 --> 00:07:51,555
Prince Chatthorn has been arrested
for embezzling funds from the ministry.

101
00:08:44,982 --> 00:08:47,531
Dad! Dad!

102
00:08:49,281 --> 00:08:50,735
Please help me!

103
00:08:57,951 --> 00:09:01,535
How could you be such a fool
and fall for that mining scheme?

104
00:09:03,109 --> 00:09:05,795
And you even used
ministry funds to invest in it?

105
00:09:06,657 --> 00:09:08,395
That was public money, you idiot!

106
00:09:10,161 --> 00:09:11,162
I'm sorry.

107
00:09:12,075 --> 00:09:14,335
It's my fault, I was so stupid.

108
00:09:15,150 --> 00:09:17,515
Please help me, I can't be in here.

109
00:09:17,555 --> 00:09:19,451
I couldn't sleep last night,
there were so many mosquitoes.

110
00:09:19,475 --> 00:09:20,795
Now you're crying.

111
00:09:21,568 --> 00:09:23,008
Why didn't you think before you acted?

112
00:09:23,539 --> 00:09:26,499
The Khana Ratsadon has been looking for
any excuse to go after the royals.

113
00:09:26,977 --> 00:09:30,435
And now the People's Committee has
more power than anyone.

114
00:09:31,179 --> 00:09:33,675
Not a single minister or director-general

115
00:09:33,697 --> 00:09:35,595
would dare step in to help.

116
00:09:39,483 --> 00:09:40,484
I…

117
00:09:41,525 --> 00:09:43,675
I looked into the documents
that the police showed.

118
00:09:45,419 --> 00:09:49,788
You're the only person who could handle pension
payments for the Department of Mineral Resources.

119
00:09:51,763 --> 00:09:54,435
If this goes to court,

120
00:09:58,675 --> 00:09:59,676
I…

121
00:10:00,494 --> 00:10:02,635
I think you will go to jail for many years.

122
00:10:03,427 --> 00:10:05,931
I can't go to jail, Tin. I really can't.

123
00:10:05,945 --> 00:10:08,321
I can't go to jail. You need to help me!

124
00:10:08,395 --> 00:10:11,355
Tin… you need to help
me! I really can't go to jail.

125
00:10:11,723 --> 00:10:13,075
Dad… please help me.

126
00:10:13,259 --> 00:10:16,115
- I can't go to jail...
- Shut up!

127
00:10:18,686 --> 00:10:22,035
You're crying and wailing like that,
aren't you ashamed?

128
00:10:25,043 --> 00:10:28,635
Have some dignity.
Act like a child of mine.

129
00:10:44,774 --> 00:10:45,775
Tin.

130
00:10:46,062 --> 00:10:47,422
- Chat.
- Tin, don't leave me here.

131
00:10:47,772 --> 00:10:50,075
Look at them! Didn't you see them?

132
00:10:50,750 --> 00:10:53,315
- Chat.
- Look at them!

133
00:10:54,915 --> 00:10:56,315
I will try to help you get out of here.

134
00:10:59,430 --> 00:11:00,635
Don't leve me here, please.

135
00:11:02,235 --> 00:11:03,875
Tin, don't leave me here.

136
00:11:04,577 --> 00:11:06,955
Look at them! Tin! Don't leave me.

137
00:11:14,443 --> 00:11:17,675
Damrong, you know someone on
the People's Committee, don't you?

138
00:11:18,785 --> 00:11:21,275
Could you use your
connections to help my son?

139
00:11:24,862 --> 00:11:27,035
You've known Chatthorn
since he was a boy, Damrong.

140
00:11:27,806 --> 00:11:29,155
He's like one of your own.

141
00:11:30,387 --> 00:11:33,075
And soon enough, we'll
be family through marriage.

142
00:11:33,918 --> 00:11:35,675
I can't help you with Chatthorn.

143
00:11:38,414 --> 00:11:42,435
About Tinnakorn and
Ruethaisiri's engagement,

144
00:11:43,915 --> 00:11:45,155
we should call it off for now.

145
00:11:47,345 --> 00:11:49,425
Why do you suddenly want
to call off the engagement?

146
00:11:50,335 --> 00:11:51,755
The country is in turmoil.

147
00:11:52,633 --> 00:11:55,634
Besides, it's not as though they'll
be getting married anytime soon.

148
00:11:56,137 --> 00:11:58,097
We might as well call off
the engagement for now.

149
00:12:00,611 --> 00:12:01,612
Uncle?

150
00:12:02,409 --> 00:12:05,155
Uncle, could you…

151
00:12:05,822 --> 00:12:07,235
- help my brother...
- Enough, Tin.

152
00:12:10,913 --> 00:12:12,833
Don't use the state of
the country as an excuse.

153
00:12:12,995 --> 00:12:14,315
Don't think I don't know that

154
00:12:14,713 --> 00:12:17,035
you've been cozying up
to the Khana Ratsadon,

155
00:12:17,267 --> 00:12:19,497
hoping to use your connections to
further your business interests.

156
00:12:19,521 --> 00:12:22,282
Is that why you want nothing more to do
with the Varakulvatin family?

157
00:12:24,417 --> 00:12:27,515
You're royalty, for God's sake,
yet you bow and scrape before commoners.

158
00:12:27,878 --> 00:12:29,075
Have you no dignity?

159
00:12:29,555 --> 00:12:31,393
Isn't it precisely because I've
been 'bowing to commoners'

160
00:12:31,417 --> 00:12:33,915
and have connections in
the the Khana Ratsadon

161
00:12:34,089 --> 00:12:35,515
that you came begging me to help?

162
00:12:36,814 --> 00:12:38,635
Your own son disgraced himself

163
00:12:39,006 --> 00:12:41,846
by stealing public money, and you
still have the nerve to criticize me?

164
00:12:42,867 --> 00:12:45,178
If you're so capable,
then find a way to help him yourselves.

165
00:12:45,202 --> 00:12:47,963
I'm staying out of this. I won't let
your mess drag me down with you.

166
00:13:04,027 --> 00:13:07,473
Why do you have to cut
ties with them like that?

167
00:13:08,129 --> 00:13:09,235
Isn't this what you wanted?

168
00:13:09,697 --> 00:13:12,097
You wanted to break off your engagement
to Tinnakorn anyway.

169
00:13:13,118 --> 00:13:14,915
I don't want to marry him

170
00:13:15,278 --> 00:13:17,918
because I don't want to force him
into a marriage he doesn't want.

171
00:13:18,067 --> 00:13:19,838
But that doesn't mean I want to cut ties
with him completely,

172
00:13:19,862 --> 00:13:23,395
especially now, when he's already down
and needs our help the most.

173
00:13:23,950 --> 00:13:25,155
You need to listen to me.

174
00:13:25,683 --> 00:13:29,275
Vasin is a is a Blue Mark.
He's on the opposite side from them.

175
00:13:29,587 --> 00:13:32,667
If we get involved with him, we'll only
end up getting into trouble ourselves.

176
00:13:32,691 --> 00:13:35,715
You used to condemn the Khana Ratsadon

177
00:13:36,435 --> 00:13:39,755
as traitors to the country.

178
00:13:41,033 --> 00:13:44,757
So why are you taking their side now?

179
00:13:46,475 --> 00:13:49,035
Or is it simply about money

180
00:13:49,811 --> 00:13:51,275
and what you stand to gain?

181
00:13:51,566 --> 00:13:53,875
Yes, it is.

182
00:13:54,091 --> 00:13:55,955
It's about our interests and our survival.

183
00:13:56,377 --> 00:13:58,870
You're a woman. What could you
possibly understand about any of this?

184
00:13:58,894 --> 00:14:00,715
Now shut your mouth and do as I say.

185
00:14:01,619 --> 00:14:05,355
From now on, stay away from Tinnakorn
and Varakulvatin family.

186
00:14:15,846 --> 00:14:17,635
No matter who we turn to for help,

187
00:14:17,647 --> 00:14:19,235
no one is willing to help us, Grandma.

188
00:14:19,737 --> 00:14:24,595
Even the royals who oppose the Khana
Ratsadon don't dare step in to help us.

189
00:14:25,211 --> 00:14:26,971
They're afraid they'll
get into trouble too.

190
00:14:27,361 --> 00:14:31,475
Does that mean there's really
nothing we can do to help Chat?

191
00:14:31,723 --> 00:14:33,755
Your Highness!

192
00:14:34,006 --> 00:14:35,008
What is going on?

193
00:14:35,777 --> 00:14:36,778
He's here.

194
00:14:37,622 --> 00:14:39,535
- He's here.
- Who's here?

195
00:14:46,267 --> 00:14:47,395
Chatthorn?

196
00:14:48,075 --> 00:14:49,515
- Chatthorn?
- Grandma.

197
00:14:49,835 --> 00:14:50,836
Darling?

198
00:14:51,155 --> 00:14:52,435
You know what?

199
00:14:52,609 --> 00:14:55,635
I couldn't sleep last night.
Look at the mosquito bites.

200
00:14:55,793 --> 00:14:57,075
How did you get here?

201
00:14:57,446 --> 00:15:00,675
That's right. Why were
you released from jail?

202
00:15:00,937 --> 00:15:01,938
Right.

203
00:15:08,931 --> 00:15:11,235
I've been appointed as counsel

204
00:15:11,558 --> 00:15:13,315
to handle this case.

205
00:15:14,273 --> 00:15:17,755
The People's Committee is concerned that
if he was sentenced outright,

206
00:15:17,990 --> 00:15:19,835
it might be seen as persecution.

207
00:15:20,443 --> 00:15:22,335
So they've decided to make an exception

208
00:15:22,433 --> 00:15:24,595
and give him chance to prove his innocence.

209
00:15:25,158 --> 00:15:26,275
An exception?

210
00:15:26,555 --> 00:15:29,956
So he isn't going to jail anymore?

211
00:15:30,406 --> 00:15:32,155
I am not going to jail,

212
00:15:32,614 --> 00:15:34,814
if we can find 200,000 baht

213
00:15:35,169 --> 00:15:37,115
to return to the ministry within two weeks.

214
00:15:38,929 --> 00:15:40,875
They only gave you two weeks?

215
00:15:41,433 --> 00:15:44,643
Yes, Your Highness. They're
already being very lenient in this case.

216
00:15:45,150 --> 00:15:46,735
Fortunately, someone spoke up for him,

217
00:15:47,769 --> 00:15:50,736
so he was given a chance
to make things right.

218
00:15:51,819 --> 00:15:54,275
Who spoke up for him?

219
00:15:57,153 --> 00:15:58,955
I'm sorry but I really can't say.

220
00:16:00,955 --> 00:16:02,235
Will you excuse me?

221
00:16:06,763 --> 00:16:07,915
Grandma,

222
00:16:08,411 --> 00:16:10,955
I miss you the most.

223
00:16:11,012 --> 00:16:13,435
I will sleep so well tonight.

224
00:16:30,734 --> 00:16:31,735
Your Highness?

225
00:16:36,923 --> 00:16:38,755
You're the one who helped Chat, aren't you?

226
00:16:43,035 --> 00:16:44,036
That's right.

227
00:16:46,219 --> 00:16:47,755
It was me who helped him out.

228
00:16:49,531 --> 00:16:51,195
But you can trust me.

229
00:16:52,566 --> 00:16:53,835
I don't have any hidden agenda.

230
00:16:54,567 --> 00:16:55,568
I didn't say anything.

231
00:16:57,681 --> 00:16:58,935
I'm here to thank you.

232
00:17:01,206 --> 00:17:04,275
By reaching out to help us
when our family has fallen on hard times,

233
00:17:05,491 --> 00:17:07,435
you may be putting
yourself at risk as well.

234
00:17:09,374 --> 00:17:11,275
I'm truly grateful. More than I can say.

235
00:17:13,225 --> 00:17:15,115
Please don't be sarcastic with me.

236
00:17:16,198 --> 00:17:17,235
I'm not being sarcastic.

237
00:17:19,395 --> 00:17:20,396
It's true.

238
00:17:22,705 --> 00:17:25,077
We don't have any power anymore.

239
00:17:26,481 --> 00:17:30,135
My dad is standing on
a different side than yours.

240
00:17:31,622 --> 00:17:33,115
If you stay involved with me,

241
00:17:34,002 --> 00:17:35,602
you'll only be putting yourself at risk.

242
00:18:05,603 --> 00:18:06,963
But I'm willing to take that risk.

243
00:18:09,310 --> 00:18:10,315
All I ask is that

244
00:18:12,121 --> 00:18:14,075
we go back to the way we were.

245
00:18:17,719 --> 00:18:18,720
Can we?

246
00:18:21,710 --> 00:18:23,355
Will you forgive me?

247
00:18:29,670 --> 00:18:31,435
There's nothing for me to forgive.

248
00:18:33,177 --> 00:18:34,435
You have your reasons,

249
00:18:35,859 --> 00:18:37,035
your beliefs,

250
00:18:39,166 --> 00:18:41,035
and the things you believe you have to do.

251
00:18:46,945 --> 00:18:49,955
We're no longer just two people
who love each other.

252
00:18:54,011 --> 00:18:55,715
You belong to the new system,

253
00:18:56,577 --> 00:18:58,195
while I am from Varakulvatin family.

254
00:18:59,483 --> 00:19:00,595
My name,

255
00:19:01,830 --> 00:19:02,831
my birth,

256
00:19:04,838 --> 00:19:05,839
my family,

257
00:19:08,579 --> 00:19:11,715
everything I am, is everything
you're trying to tear down.

258
00:19:16,371 --> 00:19:17,795
But you're not my enemy.

259
00:19:19,326 --> 00:19:21,206
I don't think the others
would see it that way.

260
00:19:22,201 --> 00:19:25,081
The Khana Ratsadon is keeping a close eye
on the royal family right now.

261
00:19:25,486 --> 00:19:27,526
My father is on the opposite
side from you as well.

262
00:19:29,547 --> 00:19:31,115
If you continue to be around with me,

263
00:19:32,370 --> 00:19:33,995
they will suspect you too.

264
00:19:35,307 --> 00:19:38,358
I don't want to be the
reason you have to choose

265
00:19:40,286 --> 00:19:41,287
between me

266
00:19:42,287 --> 00:19:43,555
and everything you believe in.

267
00:20:06,907 --> 00:20:07,908
Phob, thank you

268
00:20:11,635 --> 00:20:12,636
for everything.

269
00:21:06,220 --> 00:21:08,115
I'll be looking forward
to seeing you succeed.

270
00:21:55,046 --> 00:21:58,435
Even if we sold everything
of value in the palace,

271
00:21:59,161 --> 00:22:00,875
it still wouldn't bring in 100,000 baht.

272
00:22:04,585 --> 00:22:06,395
The economy is in bad shape right now.

273
00:22:08,606 --> 00:22:10,555
I doubt any of it will be easy to sell.

274
00:22:15,982 --> 00:22:17,475
They gave us only two weeks.

275
00:22:19,049 --> 00:22:21,097
They're deliberately trying
to back us into a corner.

276
00:22:21,121 --> 00:22:23,481
There's no way we can find
that money in such a short time.

277
00:22:39,045 --> 00:22:40,046
Actually,

278
00:22:41,150 --> 00:22:42,750
I went to see an English friend of mine.

279
00:22:45,518 --> 00:22:47,518
They are looking for a
place to turn into a hotel.

280
00:22:51,043 --> 00:22:52,435
He told me

281
00:22:54,455 --> 00:22:55,835
he'd be willing to buy our palace

282
00:22:57,761 --> 00:22:59,155
for 100,000 baht.

283
00:23:17,814 --> 00:23:19,075
Is selling this palace

284
00:23:22,385 --> 00:23:24,195
really our only option?

285
00:23:43,459 --> 00:23:44,875
Take the money

286
00:23:45,875 --> 00:23:48,315
and make a good life for yourself.

287
00:23:49,683 --> 00:23:51,835
Make an honest living,

288
00:23:52,902 --> 00:23:54,195
and take good care of yourself.

289
00:23:55,670 --> 00:23:57,595
I'm sorry.

290
00:23:59,483 --> 00:24:03,955
I couldn't take care of all
of you until the very end.

291
00:24:16,777 --> 00:24:20,115
Thank you for everything
you've done over the years,

292
00:24:20,654 --> 00:24:23,435
for taking care of this
palace and of our family.

293
00:24:27,905 --> 00:24:28,906
Aum,

294
00:24:30,115 --> 00:24:31,116
this is yours.

295
00:24:35,139 --> 00:24:36,915
I am not going anywhere.

296
00:24:39,403 --> 00:24:44,075
You've cared for me and raised me
since I was a little girl.

297
00:24:46,305 --> 00:24:49,235
Please let me go with you
and take care of you, Your Highness.

298
00:24:52,491 --> 00:24:53,675
Oh, Aum.

299
00:24:55,163 --> 00:24:56,415
I don't even know

300
00:24:58,017 --> 00:24:59,878
what our lives will be like

301
00:25:00,566 --> 00:25:02,755
from now on.

302
00:25:04,758 --> 00:25:06,801
Don't stay and suffer alongside us.

303
00:25:07,030 --> 00:25:08,485
I'm not scared of hardship.

304
00:25:09,195 --> 00:25:10,427
I'm not scared at all.

305
00:25:11,387 --> 00:25:14,755
Please let me go with
you and take care of you.

306
00:25:26,129 --> 00:25:28,335
Thank you.

307
00:26:20,923 --> 00:26:21,924
Vasin, dear.

308
00:26:40,566 --> 00:26:41,567
It's okay.

309
00:26:42,587 --> 00:26:44,155
It's going to be okay.

310
00:26:47,302 --> 00:26:48,755
We will stay together.

311
00:26:50,018 --> 00:26:51,555
We will get through this together.

312
00:26:53,272 --> 00:26:55,155
I love you, dear.

313
00:26:55,862 --> 00:26:57,395
I love you.

314
00:27:35,681 --> 00:27:39,435
I hereby appoint you as my knight.

315
00:27:40,675 --> 00:27:41,676
Thank you, Your Highness.

316
00:27:48,409 --> 00:27:51,435
May I offer you this
cotton rose, Your Highness?

317
00:27:51,961 --> 00:27:53,535
- No!
- Why not?

318
00:27:53,966 --> 00:27:54,967
I have a better idea.

319
00:27:56,643 --> 00:27:57,644
This is better.

320
00:27:58,190 --> 00:27:59,535
Oh, come on.

321
00:28:01,523 --> 00:28:02,635
Aww, so cute.

322
00:28:04,834 --> 00:28:05,835
I can't take it off?

323
00:28:05,897 --> 00:28:07,537
You can't. You have to wear it like this.

324
00:28:08,211 --> 00:28:09,595
It looks better this way.

325
00:29:06,195 --> 00:29:08,115
[Varakulvatin Palace]

326
00:29:13,801 --> 00:29:15,115
They sold Varakulvatin Palace?

327
00:29:15,785 --> 00:29:17,386
I just found out about it.

328
00:29:17,561 --> 00:29:19,801
Some foreigners bought it
and will turn it into a hotel.

329
00:29:20,395 --> 00:29:22,755
When are they moving out?
And where are they going to live?

330
00:29:23,273 --> 00:29:24,835
We don't know about that.

331
00:30:16,235 --> 00:30:17,236
Your Highness?

332
00:30:18,755 --> 00:30:19,835
Where are you now?

333
00:30:22,075 --> 00:30:23,315
But I wil find you

334
00:30:24,534 --> 00:30:25,995
no matter what.

335
00:31:33,286 --> 00:31:35,235
Do we really have to live here?

336
00:31:37,697 --> 00:31:41,835
And whose fault is it that we have no roof over
our heads and had to come all the way here?

337
00:31:41,935 --> 00:31:42,936
It's because of Phob.

338
00:31:44,043 --> 00:31:45,315
He betrayed the nation

339
00:31:45,611 --> 00:31:47,651
and seized power. That's
why we've fallen this far.

340
00:32:26,982 --> 00:32:27,983
Phob.

341
00:32:29,294 --> 00:32:31,715
What the people from
Varakulvatin family need to face

342
00:32:32,206 --> 00:32:33,595
is not your fault at all.

343
00:32:34,073 --> 00:32:35,913
You did everything in
your power to help them,

344
00:32:36,057 --> 00:32:37,977
despite drawing the
attention of your superiors.

345
00:32:40,563 --> 00:32:41,595
I once believed that

346
00:32:44,275 --> 00:32:45,790
if the world changed,

347
00:32:47,070 --> 00:32:48,395
it would become easier for us

348
00:32:49,705 --> 00:32:51,675
to love each other.

349
00:32:53,136 --> 00:32:54,315
But instead,

350
00:32:55,990 --> 00:32:59,595
it's only pushed us further apart.

351
00:33:14,358 --> 00:33:15,718
Don't get ahead of yourself, okay?

352
00:33:16,881 --> 00:33:17,882
Just stay calm,

353
00:33:18,635 --> 00:33:21,436
and we'll figure out where
Prince Tinnakorn has gone.

354
00:33:31,097 --> 00:33:32,635
Alright, let's eat.

355
00:33:33,715 --> 00:33:36,155
We'll eat what we have.

356
00:33:36,491 --> 00:33:39,009
At least we still have something to eat.

357
00:33:40,331 --> 00:33:41,332
Grandma?

358
00:33:41,435 --> 00:33:42,515
Aum, water please.

359
00:33:43,286 --> 00:33:44,595
Should you go to see a doctor?

360
00:33:45,075 --> 00:33:47,195
It's okay. I'm okay.

361
00:33:47,635 --> 00:33:49,795
It's probably from all the dust.

362
00:33:49,875 --> 00:33:51,876
I'll get better when I have some water.

363
00:33:59,809 --> 00:34:00,810
Are you feeling better?

364
00:34:01,985 --> 00:34:02,986
I'm fine.

365
00:34:04,622 --> 00:34:05,995
I'm going to Korat tomorrow.

366
00:34:07,435 --> 00:34:08,436
Why do you have to go?

367
00:34:10,505 --> 00:34:13,035
I've been asked to meet with
some members of the royal family.

368
00:34:14,635 --> 00:34:17,915
There are still many who
stand against all of this.

369
00:34:19,385 --> 00:34:21,075
Maybe there's still a chance.

370
00:34:23,193 --> 00:34:24,194
Dad,

371
00:34:25,774 --> 00:34:28,195
I don't think you should be
involved with this anymore.

372
00:34:29,982 --> 00:34:32,035
We have no money, no power,

373
00:34:32,083 --> 00:34:34,585
nothing left to fight them with.
Please don't get involved.

374
00:34:35,707 --> 00:34:37,169
I'm worried about you.

375
00:34:37,222 --> 00:34:38,223
I'm not scared.

376
00:34:40,753 --> 00:34:42,955
I refuse to let us live in such disgrace.

377
00:34:44,473 --> 00:34:46,035
I will restore the honor

378
00:34:46,766 --> 00:34:48,835
and dignity of our family.

379
00:34:51,779 --> 00:34:54,219
If our house is to fall while
I'm the one responsible for it,

380
00:34:54,376 --> 00:34:56,635
how could I ever face our ancestors?

381
00:35:01,769 --> 00:35:02,809
You need to pack your bag.

382
00:35:03,390 --> 00:35:04,391
You are coming with me.

383
00:35:05,515 --> 00:35:06,795
Do I have to come with you?

384
00:35:07,478 --> 00:35:10,515
I can't let you out of my sight,
or you'll get in trouble again.

385
00:35:18,195 --> 00:35:19,355
Let's eat.

386
00:35:21,270 --> 00:35:22,835
I want to have Gaeng Ran Juan.

387
00:35:25,608 --> 00:35:27,048
Why don't you try this soup instead?

388
00:35:27,336 --> 00:35:29,475
It's mixed veggies soup.

389
00:35:29,485 --> 00:35:31,275
Aum made it, it's tasty.

390
00:35:34,577 --> 00:35:36,195
We don't have any vacancies.

391
00:35:37,409 --> 00:35:40,875
All we have is manual
labor, do you want it?

392
00:35:41,563 --> 00:35:42,564
I'll take it.

393
00:35:42,929 --> 00:35:45,718
I'll take any job. I just need work.

394
00:35:47,339 --> 00:35:49,899
I don't think you can do it.

395
00:36:14,769 --> 00:36:16,569
Do you know how to
dye fabric, Your Highness?

396
00:36:35,417 --> 00:36:38,046
All we've got here is heavy manual work.

397
00:36:39,275 --> 00:36:40,395
Do you think you can do it?

398
00:36:46,294 --> 00:36:47,295
Yes, yes.

399
00:36:48,241 --> 00:36:49,242
I can do it.

400
00:41:08,150 --> 00:41:09,151
Oh my!

401
00:41:10,235 --> 00:41:11,236
Grandma?

402
00:41:12,955 --> 00:41:13,956
Grandma!

403
00:41:15,774 --> 00:41:16,775
What's wrong?

404
00:41:17,235 --> 00:41:18,635
It's Aum.

405
00:41:18,715 --> 00:41:21,355
I asked her to watch my
coconut milk in the pan,

406
00:41:21,510 --> 00:41:24,035
and she burned it every time.

407
00:41:24,102 --> 00:41:25,622
She's old and I'm sick of her already.

408
00:41:27,027 --> 00:41:28,955
Wait, what are you doing?

409
00:41:30,195 --> 00:41:32,675
We're making desserts.

410
00:41:36,006 --> 00:41:37,395
Is it because of me?

411
00:41:39,958 --> 00:41:41,435
I still couldn't find a job.

412
00:41:42,342 --> 00:41:44,835
And everybody has to be
in this hardship together.

413
00:41:46,202 --> 00:41:48,635
- We have to...
- Don't say that.

414
00:41:48,750 --> 00:41:51,595
Don't blame yourself, dear.

415
00:41:51,758 --> 00:41:54,635
Let me tell you something, dear.

416
00:41:54,659 --> 00:41:57,835
In life, none of us can stay
in the same place forever.

417
00:41:58,089 --> 00:41:59,649
One day you may be on top of the world,

418
00:41:59,806 --> 00:42:02,395
and the next you may fall.

419
00:42:02,649 --> 00:42:04,555
You may be crying one day

420
00:42:04,699 --> 00:42:07,075
and laughing the next.

421
00:42:07,590 --> 00:42:10,595
None of it matters.

422
00:42:10,758 --> 00:42:15,595
What truly matters is what inside here,

423
00:42:15,824 --> 00:42:18,795
whether your heart can still
pick itself up and keep fighting.

424
00:42:18,891 --> 00:42:23,115
As long as we still have
the strength to carry on

425
00:42:23,316 --> 00:42:25,068
and have breath in our lungs,

426
00:42:25,239 --> 00:42:29,278
we're already more fortunate
than so many others, my dear.

427
00:42:30,515 --> 00:42:33,315
But you've never had to
suffer like this, Grandma.

428
00:42:34,185 --> 00:42:36,115
I don't see anything wrong with that.

429
00:42:36,558 --> 00:42:39,755
It was nice having what we had before,

430
00:42:39,921 --> 00:42:44,275
but there's something good
about living like this, too.

431
00:42:44,542 --> 00:42:48,795
Now we get to understand how people

432
00:42:49,054 --> 00:42:51,195
who struggle every day actually live.

433
00:42:51,433 --> 00:42:53,595
I'm okay, I don't see it as a problem.

434
00:42:54,094 --> 00:42:55,275
I can live like this.

435
00:42:57,942 --> 00:43:03,072
I think… maybe this
isn't a punishment at all.

436
00:43:03,249 --> 00:43:06,715
Maybe it's a test or a lesson,

437
00:43:06,827 --> 00:43:10,035
and it's meant to help you

438
00:43:10,071 --> 00:43:12,454
understand the world a little better.

439
00:43:16,075 --> 00:43:17,915
I never looked at it that
way before, Grandma.

440
00:43:18,046 --> 00:43:19,838
Well, then start thinking that way now.

441
00:43:19,875 --> 00:43:23,406
You need to come here and give me a hand.

442
00:43:27,630 --> 00:43:29,515
Come on, let's try.

443
00:43:30,857 --> 00:43:32,830
- Follow me.
- I'll follow you.

444
00:43:32,857 --> 00:43:34,795
You have to grate the coconut like this.

445
00:43:34,950 --> 00:43:37,555
I'm so fed up with
Aum. She's no help at all.

446
00:43:37,718 --> 00:43:40,875
She's acting like she's an
old woman, she's forgetful.

447
00:43:41,067 --> 00:43:42,068
I'm fed up with her.

448
00:43:44,135 --> 00:43:45,955
If you called me old,

449
00:43:46,190 --> 00:43:47,695
then what about you, Your Highness?

450
00:43:47,715 --> 00:43:49,641
Are you messing with me?

451
00:43:49,646 --> 00:43:53,595
- I'll get you.
- You're still young, Your Highness.

452
00:43:53,753 --> 00:43:57,635
She burned my coconut, see? I will get her.

453
00:43:57,814 --> 00:43:59,915
- You should try.
- Can you teach me?

454
00:43:59,985 --> 00:44:03,515
Hold it with your hands
like this, use both hands.

455
00:44:03,793 --> 00:44:07,035
And you push coconut gentle like this,
don't push it too hard.

456
00:44:07,135 --> 00:44:08,136
That's right.

457
00:44:11,681 --> 00:44:13,395
Pongpang!

458
00:44:33,153 --> 00:44:34,435
Wishing you lots of sales, Aum.

459
00:44:34,475 --> 00:44:36,131
- Thank you.
- Please take care of my grandma.

460
00:44:36,155 --> 00:44:37,156
Sure, don't worry.

461
00:44:38,329 --> 00:44:39,330
Grandma,

462
00:44:39,857 --> 00:44:42,195
a school called me in
for a job interview today.

463
00:44:43,147 --> 00:44:46,835
That's great. See, I told you.

464
00:44:46,915 --> 00:44:48,875
If you don't give up,

465
00:44:48,916 --> 00:44:51,435
you will always figure something out.

466
00:44:52,275 --> 00:44:54,115
May I have your blessing, Grandma?

467
00:44:54,275 --> 00:44:55,395
Of course, you can.

468
00:44:57,675 --> 00:45:01,676
May everything go your way today,

469
00:45:01,787 --> 00:45:04,555
and may you get the job
your heart desires, my dear.

470
00:45:06,665 --> 00:45:08,755
Thank you so much, Grandma.

471
00:45:17,995 --> 00:45:20,395
- I should go.
- Good luck, dear.

472
00:45:20,696 --> 00:45:21,697
Thank you.

473
00:45:25,081 --> 00:45:27,921
[Will the people gain freedom,
or merely trade one master for another?]

474
00:45:29,169 --> 00:45:30,535
Pongpang!

475
00:45:37,483 --> 00:45:39,115
They just keep twisting the truth.

476
00:45:42,015 --> 00:45:44,815
The people haven't seen any real
results yet, so they're still afraid.

477
00:45:45,195 --> 00:45:46,995
But they're turning the people against us.

478
00:45:57,235 --> 00:45:59,236
[Wat Khlongta School]

479
00:46:02,825 --> 00:46:05,795
I never imagined we'd have
someone like you teaching at our school.

480
00:46:06,150 --> 00:46:07,355
It will be a lot of work

481
00:46:07,574 --> 00:46:09,174
because you have to teach every subject,

482
00:46:09,553 --> 00:46:11,891
especially with kids of different ages
all in the same class.

483
00:46:11,915 --> 00:46:13,835
Are you sure you can
handle this, Your Highness?

484
00:46:14,235 --> 00:46:16,035
You can call me Tinnakorn.

485
00:46:17,395 --> 00:46:18,396
As for the work,

486
00:46:18,654 --> 00:46:21,174
no matter how demanding
or exhausting it gets, I can handle it.

487
00:46:21,993 --> 00:46:24,395
Thank you so much for giving me this job.

488
00:46:33,993 --> 00:46:37,094
If you can't read or write yet,

489
00:46:37,135 --> 00:46:38,502
or if this is your first day here,

490
00:46:38,891 --> 00:46:39,931
there's no need to be shy.

491
00:46:40,011 --> 00:46:41,995
It's my first day teaching here, too.

492
00:46:44,166 --> 00:46:46,379
Today, I'm going to teach you

493
00:46:46,507 --> 00:46:48,675
how to read Thai consonants.

494
00:46:49,835 --> 00:46:52,585
These are Thai consonants.

495
00:46:52,766 --> 00:46:54,395
This is how you write the first letter.

496
00:46:54,601 --> 00:46:57,995
And it is called 'Kor.
Khai', repeat after me.

497
00:46:58,475 --> 00:47:00,121
Kor. Khai.

498
00:47:00,335 --> 00:47:01,336
Good job.

499
00:47:01,774 --> 00:47:03,275
Let's continue.

500
00:47:40,235 --> 00:47:42,935
Today, we're going to learn some math.

501
00:47:43,041 --> 00:47:45,875
Hold up your finger like
me and say the number. One.

502
00:47:46,150 --> 00:47:48,315
- One.
- Plus.

503
00:47:48,545 --> 00:47:50,609
- Plus.
- The same number.

504
00:47:50,635 --> 00:47:52,675
- One.
- One.

505
00:47:52,736 --> 00:47:54,875
- Equals…
- Two.

506
00:47:54,935 --> 00:47:56,395
That's right. It means that…

507
00:47:56,481 --> 00:47:58,515
one plus one equals two.

508
00:48:01,414 --> 00:48:02,415
H.

509
00:48:03,020 --> 00:48:04,021
K.

510
00:48:05,179 --> 00:48:07,403
A-Ant.

511
00:48:07,670 --> 00:48:08,671
Meaning?

512
00:48:09,071 --> 00:48:10,072
Ant.

513
00:48:10,080 --> 00:48:11,081
Well done.

514
00:48:16,315 --> 00:48:17,915
[Nakhon Ratchasima]

515
00:48:23,918 --> 00:48:24,919
He's here, Your Highness.

516
00:48:25,635 --> 00:48:28,555
The moment I heard you
were joining us, I rushed over.

517
00:48:29,329 --> 00:48:30,675
There are more people, Adul.

518
00:48:31,665 --> 00:48:33,635
There are still plenty of
people who oppose them.

519
00:48:34,149 --> 00:48:35,150
Those traitors

520
00:48:35,401 --> 00:48:37,195
who want to turn Siam communist

521
00:48:37,302 --> 00:48:38,603
will all meet the same fate.

522
00:48:44,078 --> 00:48:45,675
If we get rid of those rebels,

523
00:48:46,243 --> 00:48:49,283
we'll be able to go back to the palace
and live comfortably again, won't we?

524
00:49:20,635 --> 00:49:22,315
Everything is going well?

525
00:49:22,379 --> 00:49:23,841
Absolutely, sir.

526
00:49:23,974 --> 00:49:24,975
Good.

527
00:49:33,763 --> 00:49:34,764
Oh!

528
00:49:35,059 --> 00:49:36,835
Good evening, Your Highness.

529
00:49:37,166 --> 00:49:38,635
Happy birthday to you, Mr. Kitti.

530
00:49:42,025 --> 00:49:44,475
The future of Siam is in your hands now.

531
00:49:47,065 --> 00:49:48,235
Thank you, Your Highness.

532
00:49:49,043 --> 00:49:50,915
I've read the government's new laws.

533
00:49:51,470 --> 00:49:52,995
If there's anything I can do to help,

534
00:49:53,781 --> 00:49:57,075
I'd be honored to play my part
in moving our country forward.

535
00:49:58,692 --> 00:49:59,852
Of course, I'll let you know.

536
00:50:00,678 --> 00:50:02,485
We can talk about that later.

537
00:50:04,070 --> 00:50:05,115
Please enjoy the party.

538
00:50:22,089 --> 00:50:23,715
Thank you, thank you so much.

539
00:50:26,286 --> 00:50:29,235
What about the project
that we talked about?

540
00:50:30,835 --> 00:50:33,891
It's boring, right? I know.

541
00:50:37,985 --> 00:50:40,035
When we were planning
the change of government,

542
00:50:43,377 --> 00:50:45,697
I imagined a very different Siam
from the one we have now.

543
00:50:52,305 --> 00:50:53,985
The country has only just begun to change.

544
00:50:54,449 --> 00:50:57,275
You can't expect everything
to be perfect overnight.

545
00:50:57,697 --> 00:50:59,435
I'm not expecting perfection.

546
00:51:01,264 --> 00:51:04,675
I just never imagined I'd
live to see something like this.

547
00:51:07,854 --> 00:51:08,995
Are we turning into

548
00:51:11,075 --> 00:51:12,755
the very thing we fought against?

549
00:51:16,843 --> 00:51:18,355
Is everything okay?

550
00:51:23,883 --> 00:51:25,915
Are we really doing this for the people?

551
00:51:27,243 --> 00:51:28,275
What a weird question?

552
00:51:32,203 --> 00:51:35,595
People are unemployed out there.
They're angry with us.

553
00:51:36,326 --> 00:51:37,327
And here we are,

554
00:51:38,179 --> 00:51:40,335
holding a celebration as
if nothing is happening.

555
00:51:42,547 --> 00:51:45,211
People are saying we've simply
replaced the old masters with new ones.

556
00:51:45,235 --> 00:51:47,835
Politics isn't driven by ideals alone.

557
00:51:48,443 --> 00:51:49,875
But when you brought us into this,

558
00:51:50,603 --> 00:51:51,915
you spoke of ideals.

559
00:51:52,155 --> 00:51:53,969
You spoke of dignity.
You spoke of equality.

560
00:51:54,998 --> 00:51:57,302
Now it feels like we've
forgotten why we're here.

561
00:51:57,435 --> 00:51:58,436
I've never forgotten.

562
00:52:00,411 --> 00:52:03,262
You can't govern a country with beautiful
ideals written on a piece of paper.

563
00:52:03,286 --> 00:52:05,715
We have to make
compromises, forge alliances,

564
00:52:05,899 --> 00:52:07,529
and bring those with power to our side.

565
00:52:08,025 --> 00:52:11,155
Otherwise, the government won't survive,
and the country won't move forward.

566
00:52:13,091 --> 00:52:14,891
And what about the
people who believed in us?

567
00:52:16,227 --> 00:52:17,795
The people who put their hopes in us?

568
00:52:18,798 --> 00:52:20,678
How many more years do
you expect them to wait?

569
00:52:21,481 --> 00:52:23,275
Do you really think you
can change a country

570
00:52:24,339 --> 00:52:25,659
without getting your hands dirty?

571
00:52:26,920 --> 00:52:27,921
If you do,

572
00:52:30,192 --> 00:52:32,035
you're far too naive.

573
00:52:39,387 --> 00:52:40,388
This way, sir.

574
00:52:41,771 --> 00:52:42,915
Happy birthday, sir.

575
00:52:43,057 --> 00:52:46,035
Thank you, thank you so much.

576
00:52:46,315 --> 00:52:47,316
Thank you.

577
00:52:49,384 --> 00:52:50,385
Thank you everyone.

578
00:54:29,129 --> 00:54:31,515
Hello, Mr. Tin.

579
00:54:31,865 --> 00:54:33,891
Whoa! There are a lot of fruits.

580
00:54:34,121 --> 00:54:37,435
The students gave me a lot of fruit,
so I thought I'd share some with you.

581
00:54:37,705 --> 00:54:39,315
These rambutans are from Sompol.

582
00:54:39,731 --> 00:54:41,675
Mangosteens are from Niyom's orchard.

583
00:54:41,833 --> 00:54:43,995
And I think Santols are from Noknoi.

584
00:54:44,601 --> 00:54:46,075
You remember them all?

585
00:54:46,446 --> 00:54:49,275
I used to buy fruit and vegetables
from their parents all the time.

586
00:54:50,067 --> 00:54:51,793
Then they started
sending their kids to school.

587
00:54:51,817 --> 00:54:54,355
I've gone from being their
customer to their teacher.

588
00:54:56,371 --> 00:54:57,372
Right.

589
00:54:58,635 --> 00:54:59,636
Yeah?

590
00:54:59,689 --> 00:55:01,335
The ministry wanted us to explain

591
00:55:01,355 --> 00:55:03,035
the new government system to the students.

592
00:55:06,875 --> 00:55:09,235
[The People's Party
Proclamation of 1932, No. 1]

593
00:55:15,358 --> 00:55:16,835
It used to be quiet around here,

594
00:55:18,014 --> 00:55:20,254
but these days, more and
more kids are coming to school.

595
00:55:20,851 --> 00:55:22,515
Their parents sent their kids to school,

596
00:55:22,774 --> 00:55:24,635
they want them to learn to read and write,

597
00:55:24,655 --> 00:55:26,695
so they can have an
easier life than their parents.

598
00:55:27,835 --> 00:55:30,955
It's a good thing the government
is putting money into education.

599
00:55:32,441 --> 00:55:34,755
I don't know where
all this politics is going,

600
00:55:35,518 --> 00:55:36,595
but as long as

601
00:55:36,750 --> 00:55:40,115
the kids are getting an education,
I suppose things can't be all that bad.

602
00:55:59,291 --> 00:56:02,153
Mr. Tin, can you check this
for me? Did I get it right?

603
00:56:02,185 --> 00:56:03,186
Let me see.

604
00:56:03,993 --> 00:56:07,875
"When I grow up, I want to
be like my teacher, Mr. Tin."

605
00:56:09,475 --> 00:56:12,715
"So I don't have to work
in the fields or on a farm."

606
00:56:13,670 --> 00:56:15,715
"I can have money to
take care of my grandma,"

607
00:56:16,091 --> 00:56:18,155
"and my mom, who's sick at home."

608
00:56:19,089 --> 00:56:20,485
"I want to be a good person."

609
00:56:23,929 --> 00:56:25,289
Excellent! You got them all right.

610
00:56:25,347 --> 00:56:26,348
Thank you.

611
00:56:27,369 --> 00:56:29,370
- You can continue writing.
- Okay.

612
00:56:29,619 --> 00:56:31,035
I'll do my very best.

613
00:56:31,513 --> 00:56:32,514
Keep it up.

614
00:56:50,534 --> 00:56:52,955
- Phob.
- Hello, Janthorn.

615
00:56:55,758 --> 00:56:59,515
Auntie, can I trouble you
for another meal today?

616
00:56:59,721 --> 00:57:00,722
Sure, you can.

617
00:57:01,577 --> 00:57:03,576
What do you have here?

618
00:57:04,990 --> 00:57:08,110
Someone at the printing house brought
this for me. They said it's really good.

619
00:57:10,494 --> 00:57:12,955
It looks so good.

620
00:57:21,566 --> 00:57:22,835
This dessert

621
00:57:24,567 --> 00:57:26,247
reminds me of the one that the Princess made.

622
00:57:28,571 --> 00:57:31,355
I used to help her back then.

623
00:57:33,955 --> 00:57:36,355
I have no idea

624
00:57:37,310 --> 00:57:38,875
how they are doing right now.

625
00:57:47,987 --> 00:57:50,635
Can I help you in the kitchen today?

626
00:57:50,894 --> 00:57:52,974
Maybe some of your cooking
magic will rub off on me.

627
00:57:53,262 --> 00:57:54,263
Let's go.

628
00:58:28,918 --> 00:58:29,919
I'm here.

629
00:58:36,019 --> 00:58:37,020
Wow!

630
00:58:38,206 --> 00:58:39,207
Thank you, Your Highness.

631
00:58:39,859 --> 00:58:41,595
I helped Grandma make some desserts.

632
00:58:48,937 --> 00:58:49,938
I…

633
00:58:51,966 --> 00:58:53,275
Let me guess.

634
00:58:54,638 --> 00:58:55,639
This is the one

635
00:58:57,078 --> 00:58:58,315
that you made, isn't it?

636
00:59:00,038 --> 00:59:01,039
How did you know?

637
00:59:01,179 --> 00:59:04,195
It's bigger than the rest.

638
00:59:04,523 --> 00:59:05,643
And the color is too bright.

639
00:59:06,118 --> 00:59:07,875
I don't think your grandma made this one.

640
00:59:09,766 --> 00:59:10,915
You don't have to eat them.

641
00:59:11,078 --> 00:59:12,859
Oh, come on.

642
00:59:13,254 --> 00:59:14,635
I am starving.

643
00:59:15,201 --> 00:59:19,075
They're huge, misshapen,
and look ridiculous.

644
00:59:19,281 --> 00:59:21,562
You'll only end up with an
upset stomach. Don't eat them.

645
00:59:22,011 --> 00:59:24,675
Oh, Your Highness. Come on.

646
00:59:25,072 --> 00:59:26,073
I was just joking.

647
00:59:29,638 --> 00:59:30,639
Well.

648
00:59:32,321 --> 00:59:35,235
They may look a little strange,

649
00:59:36,161 --> 00:59:38,121
but I think they'll be
the most delicious of all.

650
00:59:39,755 --> 00:59:42,335
Stop trying, it won't work.

651
00:59:50,171 --> 00:59:51,755
- Is it good?
- It's good.

652
00:59:53,446 --> 00:59:54,447
This is the best.

653
00:59:55,439 --> 00:59:56,999
Then you should sit properly to eat it.

654
01:00:02,366 --> 01:00:03,395
This is so good.

655
01:00:03,459 --> 01:00:05,115
- Let me try.
- I'll feed you.

656
01:00:12,830 --> 01:00:13,831
What do you think?

657
01:00:14,606 --> 01:00:15,607
It is good.

658
01:00:16,073 --> 01:00:17,074
Because?

659
01:00:17,523 --> 01:00:18,995
Because this isn't the one I made.

660
01:00:27,835 --> 01:00:29,235
[Constitutional Government
Knowledge Contest]

661
01:00:29,245 --> 01:00:31,805
[Organized by Ministry of Public
Instruction — December 8, 1932]

662
01:00:35,046 --> 01:00:36,275
Their school is so nice.

663
01:00:37,542 --> 01:00:38,543
Don't be cared.

664
01:00:39,393 --> 01:00:41,715
Believe in yourself. You can do it.

665
01:00:42,369 --> 01:00:44,609
I'm so nervous I feel like
I'm going to pee myself, sir.

666
01:00:45,291 --> 01:00:47,075
We should get going.

667
01:00:47,455 --> 01:00:50,003
At this rate, you'll end up answering questions
and peeing your pants at the same time.

668
01:00:50,027 --> 01:00:52,166
If you'll excuse us, we'd
better go to the bathroom.

669
01:00:52,267 --> 01:00:54,195
Of course. Go ahead and
use the bathroom first.

670
01:00:54,838 --> 01:00:56,035
Let's go.

671
01:01:33,329 --> 01:01:34,330
Your Highness,

672
01:01:39,305 --> 01:01:40,435
what are you doing here?

673
01:01:44,355 --> 01:01:46,335
I'm here with my students
for a quiz competition.

674
01:01:48,057 --> 01:01:49,058
Your students?

675
01:01:51,795 --> 01:01:52,796
Right,

676
01:01:53,347 --> 01:01:55,795
I am a teacher... Mr. Tin.

677
01:01:59,057 --> 01:02:00,058
What about you?

678
01:02:04,241 --> 01:02:05,635
I'm representing my department

679
01:02:06,843 --> 01:02:09,035
on the judging panel, Your Highness.

680
01:02:20,691 --> 01:02:22,315
I hope you're doing well.

681
01:02:24,691 --> 01:02:25,692
I am doing well, thanks.

682
01:02:28,435 --> 01:02:29,436
And you?

683
01:02:34,579 --> 01:02:35,580
I…

684
01:02:37,571 --> 01:02:38,572
I'm fine, I guess.

685
01:02:44,539 --> 01:02:46,339
You don't seem to be
doing too well yourself.

686
01:02:47,298 --> 01:02:48,299
Is everything okay?

687
01:02:56,686 --> 01:02:57,795
We're being criticized

688
01:02:58,638 --> 01:03:00,675
for acting too hastily and

689
01:03:02,043 --> 01:03:03,044
being too impatient,

690
01:03:04,014 --> 01:03:06,534
for pushing through change
before the country was ready for it.

691
01:03:08,542 --> 01:03:09,795
At first,

692
01:03:11,163 --> 01:03:12,275
I thought that

693
01:03:13,345 --> 01:03:14,595
after we'd changed the system,

694
01:03:15,937 --> 01:03:17,485
many things would improve.

695
01:03:19,142 --> 01:03:20,143
But even now,

696
01:03:21,321 --> 01:03:22,441
people are still struggling.

697
01:03:24,249 --> 01:03:25,889
There are still those competing for power

698
01:03:28,291 --> 01:03:30,691
and those taking advantage
of the situation, just as before.

699
01:03:35,235 --> 01:03:36,236
Sometimes.

700
01:03:37,691 --> 01:03:38,955
I can't help but wonder...

701
01:03:42,587 --> 01:03:44,335
was everything I lost

702
01:03:47,462 --> 01:03:48,875
really worth it?

703
01:03:54,267 --> 01:03:55,935
It doesn't matter anymore

704
01:03:58,150 --> 01:03:59,790
whether it happened too soon or too late.

705
01:04:02,801 --> 01:04:04,515
The change has already happened.

706
01:04:07,403 --> 01:04:10,595
What matters now is what
we do to make things better.

707
01:04:17,766 --> 01:04:18,767
You're right.

708
01:04:20,395 --> 01:04:21,855
I'm still trying to figure out

709
01:04:22,931 --> 01:04:24,235
what I should do.

710
01:04:26,798 --> 01:04:27,955
I still have my doubts.

711
01:04:29,135 --> 01:04:30,136
Phob.

712
01:04:32,635 --> 01:04:34,395
We can't always have things go our way.

713
01:04:35,926 --> 01:04:36,927
Look at me.

714
01:04:38,566 --> 01:04:43,621
I used to think my life
had already been mapped out for me.

715
01:04:46,043 --> 01:04:48,083
And yet, here I am, having
to start all over again.

716
01:04:50,795 --> 01:04:51,796
And you know what?

717
01:04:53,606 --> 01:04:54,886
Some of the students in my class

718
01:04:57,085 --> 01:05:00,035
couldn't even write
their own names at first.

719
01:05:01,635 --> 01:05:03,916
Some of them almost never
got the chance to go to school.

720
01:05:05,097 --> 01:05:06,665
But now they can read

721
01:05:08,617 --> 01:05:09,755
and write.

722
01:05:12,139 --> 01:05:13,499
They dare to think for themselves.

723
01:05:15,553 --> 01:05:16,595
They dare to dream.

724
01:05:18,923 --> 01:05:20,555
Maybe what you've done

725
01:05:22,152 --> 01:05:24,153
hasn't made a difference
on a larger scale yet.

726
01:05:27,235 --> 01:05:28,275
But at the very least...

727
01:05:31,669 --> 01:05:32,670
it's already beginning

728
01:05:33,659 --> 01:05:35,535
to make a difference in someone's life.

729
01:05:43,406 --> 01:05:44,485
I am rooting for you.

730
01:05:46,547 --> 01:05:47,667
Don't give up on your dream.

731
01:05:54,553 --> 01:05:56,084
You look so strong.

732
01:05:57,646 --> 01:05:59,555
I'm just trying to keep moving forward.

733
01:06:02,329 --> 01:06:03,330
You should too.

734
01:06:06,969 --> 01:06:07,970
Stay strong,

735
01:06:11,438 --> 01:06:12,439
all right?

736
01:06:30,121 --> 01:06:32,574
I need to get going.

737
01:06:34,350 --> 01:06:35,470
I wish you the best of luck.

738
01:06:36,537 --> 01:06:37,538
I'll see you later.

739
01:06:39,301 --> 01:06:40,461
See you later, Your Highness.

740
01:07:40,000 --> 01:07:44,700
(Next Episode) If I get another chance, I want His
Highness to open his heart to me a little more.

741
01:07:44,900 --> 01:07:47,400
I still want to walk side by side with him.

742
01:07:48,200 --> 01:07:51,700
This cotton rose... does
it make you miss him?

743
01:07:53,500 --> 01:07:55,999
Reports indicate that
there is suspicious movement going on.

744
01:07:56,000 --> 01:07:58,400
It seems that this time,
His Royal Highness is truly serious.

745
01:07:59,600 --> 01:08:00,600
Thin!

746
01:08:00,900 --> 01:08:03,600
Before long, everything will return to
the way it was.

747
01:08:03,900 --> 01:08:05,400
Father, what are you planning to do?

748
01:08:08,400 --> 01:08:10,200
Your Highness, is something wrong?

749
01:08:11,000 --> 01:08:12,000
Phob...
